      sources: "Sources: Learn, PIM for Groups overview and settings; Update rules; Rules mapping guide; request resource types; Update-MgPolicyRoleManagementPolicyRule. Chapter 05, “Verified facts.”",
      say: `Learn isn't always consistent with itself, and the chapter writes down every place it isn't, so a later edit doesn't quietly loosen the code. Activation length is one. Whether PIM for Groups is generally available or still beta is another: the API pages say one thing, a how-to says another. The permissions for role-assignable groups differ between pages, and the Lab 2 run is how you settle that. Even the obvious PowerShell cmdlet disagrees with its own API page, so the code calls the API directly.`,
      detail: `Where Learn's pages differ, recorded so a later edit doesn't loosen the code. Activation length: eight hours in the Graph overview, 24 in the settings page; the code caps at eight (research gaps, row 54). v1.0 or beta: the PIM for Groups API pages are v1.0; the Update rules how-to says PIM for Groups is beta only, and the PIM for Groups settings page shows a beta request; the deployment plan still links PIM for Groups as a preview; the code uses v1.0 (research gaps, row 55). Permissions for role-assignable groups: RoleManagement.ReadWrite.Directory on the role-assignable groups page; the AzureADGroup permissions on the PIM for Groups pages; the code declares the latter and Lab 2 checks it (research gaps, row 53). Creating a role-assignable group: visibility Hidden or Private (the group resource page gives both), and whether it can have owners, differ across three pages; Learn's own PowerShell for it signs in with Group.ReadWrite.All only; the code declares both Group.Create and RoleManagement.ReadWrite.Directory (research gaps, row 56). The rule cmdlet: Update-MgPolicyRoleManagementPolicyRule lists only the Directory permissions and no application support, while the API page lists RoleManagementPolicy.ReadWrite.AzureADGroup for applications; the code calls the REST API (research gaps, row 59). Also verified: Update unifiedRoleManagementPolicyRule (groups), PATCH /policies/roleManagementPolicies/{id}/rules/{id}, RoleManagementPolicy.ReadWrite.AzureADGroup, @odata.type required in the body, 17 rules per policy (v1.0). isValidationOnly: on both request types; documented for checking an activation before submitting it (v1.0).`,
      cite: ["pa05-overview", "pa05-settings", "pa05-rules-howto", "pa05-pim-plan", "pa05-group-visibility", "pa05-rag-create", "pa05-cmdlet", "pa05-rule-update", "pa05-rules-overview", "pa05-req-resource"],
      ref: "“Verified facts”",
