      sources: "Sources: Chapter 05, “Dangers”; Learn, Use Microsoft Entra groups to manage role assignments.",
      say: `Each of these dangers has a matching rule or guard. The quietest is drift: someone changes membership in the portal, and nobody ever reviews it, so every run reads first and flags what it didn't grant. The sharpest is dropping approval on a top-tier group, which Learn specifically warns lets a lesser admin act on someone else's behalf. And the bluntest is a truncated file that would remove everyone, which is why removals go last and a guard stops more than a handful. Notice again: each guard is code that runs every time.`,
      detail: `A sample copied as published: an ownership grant becomes a membership, or a 2023 date fails, or is edited by hand; guard: requests come from the file, and tests pin the sample's mismatches. A change made in the admin center or the groups API: the tenant drifts from the file and nobody reviews it; guard: every run reads first; PA-PG-09 and a removal in the plan. Approval dropped on a T0 or T1 group: a less-privileged admin who can reset a member's credentials activates on their behalf, the case Learn warns about; guard: PA-PG-08 and guard G1. A permanent member or owner: standing privilege through the group; guard: PA-PG-06 and G2. Eligible owner, no active owner: the owner activates and can't be deactivated; guard: PA-PG-07 and G4. A group nested in a PRV group: its people hold the role and the review shows a group; guard: PA-PG-05 and G5. A truncated or wrong file: the plan removes everyone; guard: removals come last, and G6 stops more than five. A non-role-assignable group used for a role: it can't hold the role, and can't be converted; guard: PA-PG-02 Finding, and the plan creates groups as role-assignable. The 500-group limit: new PRV groups can't be created; guard: PA-PG-04 Warn at 450. A pipeline app with RoleManagement.ReadWrite.Directory: it can assign any directory role; guard: group creation is planned, not routinely applied, and the plan lists only its own permissions. Names in output: diff.txt and findings.json name privileged holders; treat the run folder as evidence and delete lab copies.`,
